    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate is necessary to ensure that your motorcycle meets the necessary environmental standards. This document proves that your bike is in good condition and complies with local regulations.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">It is mandatory to have a valid insurance certificate for your motorcycle before transportation. Make sure to provide a photocopy of the insurance policy, which covers your bike during transit.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA-Approved Consignment Bill of Lading:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">To ensure a reliable and safe transportation process, it is advisable to use an IBA (Indian Bike Association) approved consignment bill of lading. This document details the shipment information, including the sender and receiver addresses, bike details, and transportation details.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #ec489922; color: #ec4899; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">05</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Declaration of 100% Declared Value Marine Transit Insurance:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">To protect your motorcycle during transportation, it is essential to opt for a 100% declared value marine transit insurance. This comprehensive insurance policy covers any potential damages or losses during transit, offering peace of mind for a safe delivery of your bike.</p>
  </div>
</div><ol>
			<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Original RC:</strong> Although not explicitly mentioned in the above list, it is important to ensure that the original Registration Certificate (RC) is available for inspection at the time of transportation. This original document is required to complete the transportation formalities.</span></li>
			<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>PUC Validity:</strong> Ensure that the Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate provided is valid and not expired. The PUC certificate confirms that your bike has passed the necessary environmental tests and is in a safe condition for transportation.</span></li>
			<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Insurance Policy Details:</strong> Kindly provide the details of your insurance policy, including the insurer's name, policy number, and contact information. This information will be required by the transport company to ensure cover for your bike during transit.</span></li>
		</ol>
		<p>By preparing and presenting the aforementioned documents, you can ensure a smooth and hassle-free bike transportation process in Valparai. It is recommended to verify the transport company's requirements beforehand to avoid any last-minute complications. Always ensure that all documents are original and up-to-date to facilitate a seamless transportation process.</p>
		<p>The IBA-approved consignment bill of lading provides a comprehensive overview of the bike details, including the make, model, and condition. Additionally, this document outlines the shipping terms, transit time, and insurance coverage.</p>
		<p>The 100% declared value marine transit insurance ensures that in case of any damages or loss during transportation, you will receive compensation based on the declared bike value.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Valparai</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle arrives at the destination, the delivery handover follows a strict, three‑step protocol to ensure transparency, accuracy, and customer confidence.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The process begins with a daylight condition re‑inspection, proceeds to odometer verification, and concludes with a signed condition sign‑off.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Each step is documented and signed by the carrier, the receiving agent, and the customer to create a tamper‑evident audit trail.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑Inspection</strong>
<ul>
<li>Both parties inspect the vehicle under natural lighting to avoid shadows or glare that could mask dents, scratches, or paint defects.</li>
<li>The carrier presents the original pickup photographs as a reference and the customer confirms that the current condition matches the images.</li>
<li>Any discrepancies are recorded in a “Condition Discrepancy Log” and photographed for evidence.</li>
</ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Odometer Verification Against LR Bilty</strong>
<ul>
<li>The carrier reads the odometer and records the mileage on the “Odometer Verification Sheet.”</li>
<li>Simultaneously, the carrier cross‑checks the reading with the mileage noted on the LR bilty and the shipment manifest.</li>
<li>Any variance exceeding 5 km triggers an immediate audit; the carrier explains the cause and the receiving agent signs a “Variance Acceptance” form if the difference is justified.</li>
</ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑Off</strong>
<ul>
<li>After the condition and odometer checks, all parties sign the “Delivery Handover Form.”</li>
<li>The form includes the vehicle’s VIN, model, color, and any noted damages, ensuring that the customer formally acknowledges receipt in the documented state.</li>
<li>Electronic copies are emailed to the carrier’s compliance team, while hard copies are kept in the customer’s file and the carrier’s records for a minimum of 90 days.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>

<p>By adhering to these steps, the carrier guarantees that the motorcycle’s condition and mileage are accurately recorded, any anomalies are transparently documented, and the customer’s signature confirms satisfaction with the delivery. This rigorous handover protocol protects all stakeholders and upholds the company’s reputation for reliability and accountability.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



